 "what": "every endpoint with negative slack in the routed timing analysis (after the router) of the seeds of the fb1dd5aa DDR3 matvec sweep that miss 83.33 MHz; an analysis, not a build",
 "sweep": "reports/fpga/ddr3-seed-sweep-2026-09-25-fb1dd5aa-x16-matvec.json",
 "netlist_sha256": "519f08021380e79ec2abed8c8555e5e2baac5856c3a254ce0d635ebb994b1e65",
 "chipdb_sha256": "5c88a26d973bff2fc33582f3937cc07d30bfc397ebae16d69a18fe49a14786a7",
 "tool": "nextpnr-xilinx 0.9.7 (0eae9fbb) with the local logging patch below, run as the sweep's command line with NEXTPNR_PRINT_NEG_SLACK=1; the patch only logs, and each run's FASM sha256 equals the sweep's for the same seed (fasm_equals_sweep), so the placements and routes are the sweep's",
 "patch": "--- a/common/timing.cc\n+++ b/common/timing.cc\n@@ #include \"timing.h\"\n+#include <cstdlib>\n@@ (the slack histogram of the final analysis)\n                             if (slack_histogram) {\n                                 int slack_ps = ctx->getDelayNS(path_budget) * 1000;\n                                 (*slack_histogram)[slack_ps]++;\n+                                // Local analysis patch (not upstream): every endpoint with negative slack.\n+                                if (slack_ps < 0 && getenv(\"NEXTPNR_PRINT_NEG_SLACK\"))\n+                                    log_info(\"NEGSLACK %d %s %s %s\\n\", slack_ps, usr.cell->name.c_str(ctx),\n+                                             usr.port.c_str(ctx), net->name.c_str(ctx));\n                             }\n",
 "source": "the cell's src attribute in the netlist (first file:line); part: UberDDR3 controller (ddr3_controller.v), loader (fpga_ddr3_loader.v, the t27 loader's on_clock block or a function), device matvec (fpga_ddr3_matvec.v)",
